# Mi Pad 2 recovery tools

`sudo mp2-backup` saves the separate `/boot` FAT filesystem and creates a
BTRFS Timeshift snapshot of the root filesystem.

`sudo mp2-recover --status` lists snapshots. `sudo mp2-recover` selects the
newest snapshot and requires typing `RECOVER` before restoring it. The
non-interactive form is `sudo mp2-recover --yes`.

The tools are local-console tools and do not depend on Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, or
SSH. They are suitable for use from the USB ACM serial console.
